        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>I will calmly read all the threatening letters and await the court case against me. But I will take a stand even if our government won’t</p><p>I can’t even remember when I decided to stop paying the sewage element of my Thames Water bill. It might have been after reading this headline from the Guardian in July 2025: “<a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2025/jul/18/serious-pollution-incidents-englands-water-companies-data\">Serious pollution incidents by English water companies rose 60% last year</a>,” with the subheading: “Environment Agency records 75 serious incidents among total of 2,800, with Thames Water being worst offender.”</p><p>Living in London means that my supplier is Thames Water, which makes a profit out of pollution. I decided that if the government wouldn’t act, I could at least do my part and not pay for this travesty.</p><p>Jenny Jones is a Green party peer</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/sep/02/thames-water-sewage-charge-bill-pollute-britain-river-coastline\">Continue reading...</a>"
